IMPORT prelude

-- First Home Owner Grant and Shared Equity Act 2000 (NSW), Part 2 -- the first home owner grant. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE.
--
-- The rules here are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "the applicant", "joint applicants", "the applicant's
-- spouse", "the Chief Commissioner" (of State Revenue). The questions of the person applying for the grant are in
-- fhog-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module, builds its records from plain answers and restates no rule.
--
-- Where the text states a duty with a deadline (ss 14(5), 20(2), (2A), (3), 21(2), (3)) or a power over the applicant
-- (s 45), it is a regulative rule (`DEONTIC`), with the applicants as parties, so that the seat is a parameter. The
-- computations (the cap, the total value, the amount, the dates) are functions.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 4A (new home); s 5 (owner, relevant interest); s 6 (spouse); s 7 (entitlement); ss 8, 8A, 9, 10,
-- 11, 12 (the eligibility criteria); s 13 (eligible transaction, commencement date, completion, consideration); s 13AA
-- (builder's and purchaser's grants); s 13A (eligibility caps); s 13B (total value); s 14(5), (6) (the application
-- period); s 15 (all interested persons to apply, with the s 15(2)(e) small interest holder); s 18 (amount); s 20(1)-(4)
-- (payment in advance and its statutory conditions); s 21(2)-(4) (conditions imposed by the Chief Commissioner; joint
-- liability); s 45(1)-(3) (repayment and penalty).
--
-- Edition: act-2000-021, corpus version 2023-09-04, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/act-2000-021.txt, taken from the Open Australian Legal Corpus (version 7.1.0; NSW
-- Legislation collected 10 March 2025). IT IS NOT THE CURRENT OFFICIAL TEXT AND MAY BE OUT OF DATE: check
-- legislation.nsw.gov.au before relying on anything here. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website
-- (State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0); see SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
--
-- NOT COVERED (answered `not covered`, never guessed): a commencement date before 1 October 2012, or a contract the Chief
-- Commissioner is satisfied replaces one made before 1 July 2017 (Schedule 1 Parts 11, 12 and 14 keep the earlier law);
-- the eligibility cap for a commencement date before 1 July 2017 (Schedule 1 Part 14); a regulation under s 13A(4) whose
-- cap was not given (none is deposited); anything that turns on the "corresponding law" of another State or a Territory
-- (ss 10, 11), which is not deposited.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part 2A (shared equity schemes); s 43A (the ADF home buyer's grant, in force on the face of the deposit);
-- Parts 2B and 3 (objections, review, investigations); ss 6A-6D and 13(6) (multiple occupancy, homes on another's land,
-- manufactured and moveable homes); s 14(1)-(4), (7) (form and information); s 16 (guardians); s 19 (how paid); s 22
-- (death of an applicant); ss 23, 24 (correcting decisions, notice); s 44 (false information); ss 46, 46A (recovery,
-- charge on the home, third parties); administration and regulations.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline,
-- no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `First Home Owner Grant and Shared Equity Act 2000 (NSW) -- the first home owner grant`

§§ `Answers this encoding does not cover`

-- The stable l4 has no REFUSE. A rule that can reach a gap answers `not covered`, with the reason.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- Schedule 1 cl 18: "Part 2 of this Act, as in force immediately before its amendment by the State Revenue and Other
    -- Legislation Amendment (Budget Measures) Act 2012, continues to apply" to contracts made, and owner builds begun,
    -- before 1 October 2012. That earlier Part 2 is not in the deposit.
    `the commencement date is before 1 October 2012, and Schedule 1 Part 11 keeps the earlier Part 2, which is not deposited`
    -- s 13(3A), Schedule 1 cl 19 (before 1 October 2012), cl 20(3) (before 1 July 2014) and cl 22(2) (before 1 July 2017):
    -- a contract the Chief Commissioner is satisfied replaces an earlier one is governed by the earlier law.
    `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces one made before 1 July 2017, and Schedule 1 keeps the earlier law, which is not encoded`
    -- s 13A(5) and Schedule 1 cl 22(1): for a commencement date before 1 July 2017 "the transitional provisions in
    -- Schedule 1 apply"; they preserve caps that are not in the deposited text.
    `the commencement date is before 1 July 2017, and Schedule 1 keeps the earlier eligibility caps, which are not encoded`
    -- s 13A(4): "The regulations may prescribe a different amount as the eligibility cap". No regulation is deposited.
    `a regulation under s 13A(4) sets a different eligibility cap, and its amount was not given (no regulation is deposited)`
    -- ss 10(1)(a), 11(1)(b), 11(3)(a): "a corresponding law" is "an Act of another State, or a Territory, corresponding to
    -- this Act" (s 3). None is deposited.
    `it turns on the corresponding law of another State or a Territory, which is not deposited`
    -- Used by a question that asks about fewer people than the application has.
    `the application has more applicants, spouses or de facto partners than this question asks about`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

-- Three-valued logic for answers that can be `not covered`. A definite "no" settles a conjunction and a definite "yes" a
-- disjunction even when the other side is not covered; otherwise a gap carries through.
GIVEN `x` IS AN `Answer` BOOLEAN, `y` IS AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`x` `and also` `y` MEANS
    CONSIDER `x`
    WHEN `answered` `p` THEN
        IF `p` THEN `y` ELSE `answered` FALSE
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN
        CONSIDER `y`
        WHEN `answered` `q` THEN
            IF `q` THEN `x` ELSE `answered` FALSE
        WHEN `not covered` `other` THEN `x`

GIVEN `x` IS AN `Answer` BOOLEAN, `y` IS AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`x` `or else` `y` MEANS
    CONSIDER `x`
    WHEN `answered` `p` THEN
        IF `p` THEN `answered` TRUE ELSE `y`
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN
        CONSIDER `y`
        WHEN `answered` `q` THEN
            IF `q` THEN `answered` TRUE ELSE `x`
        WHEN `not covered` `other` THEN `x`

GIVEN `x` IS AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`the opposite of` `x` MEANS
    CONSIDER `x`
    WHEN `answered` `p` THEN `answered` (NOT `p`)
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`

GIVEN `b` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`known` `b` MEANS `answered` `b`

GIVEN `answers` IS A LIST OF `Answer` BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`all of` `answers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `answers`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `answered` TRUE
    WHEN `first` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN `first` `and also` (`all of` `rest`)

GIVEN `answers` IS A LIST OF `Answer` BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`any of` `answers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `answers`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `answered` FALSE
    WHEN `first` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN `first` `or else` (`any of` `rest`)

§§ `Dates`

-- A period of months "after" a day ends on the same day of the later month (Interpretation Act 1987 reckoning, the day
-- itself excluded). READING: 29 February moves to 28 February in a year that has none.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`12 months after` `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2 AND DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 29
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1)

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus` `n` `days` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a` `is on or before` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a` `is before` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `a` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `a` `to` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `b` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `a`

-- s 11(1): "before 1 July 2000". s 13(1): "on or after 1 October 2012". s 18(1): "before 1 January 2016", "on or after
-- 1 January 2016". s 13A(5): "on or after 1 July 2017".
`1 July 2000`    MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2000
`1 October 2012` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2012
`1 January 2016` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2016
`1 July 2017`    MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2017

§§ `s 4A -- new homes`

-- s 4A(1): "A new home is a home that has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence, and includes a
-- substantially renovated home and a home built to replace demolished premises." (2): a substantially renovated home is
-- one "created through renovations in which all, or substantially all, of a building is removed or replaced" and "as
-- renovated, has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence". (3): a home built to replace demolished
-- premises "on the same land" that, "as built", has not been previously occupied or sold, where "(c) the owner of the home
-- did not occupy the demolished premises as a place of residence before they were demolished".
DECLARE `Origin of the home` IS ONE OF
    `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises`
    `a substantially renovated home`
    `a home built to replace demolished premises on the same land`

-- `has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence` is asked of the home as it now stands: as renovated,
-- or as built to replace the demolished premises.
-- READING: s 4A(3)(c) is applied as a condition on a replacement home, so that it has work to do. On the literal words a
-- newly built replacement home never occupied or sold is also "a home that has not been previously occupied or sold"
-- under s 4A(1), and (3)(c) would change nothing (NOTES.md finding 3).
GIVEN `the origin` IS AN `Origin of the home`
      `previously occupied or sold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner occupied the demolished premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a new home` IF
        (NOT `previously occupied or sold`)
    AND CONSIDER `the origin`
        WHEN `a home built to replace demolished premises on the same land` THEN NOT `the owner occupied the demolished premises`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 5 -- owners and relevant interests`

-- s 5(1): "A person is an owner of a home or a home owner if the person has a relevant interest in land on which a home
-- is built." s 5(2): the relevant interests. Where the Chief Commissioner must approve, be satisfied or hold an opinion,
-- the kind of interest is chosen only if that has happened.
DECLARE `Kind of interest in land` IS ONE OF
    `an estate in fee simple`                                                                            -- (2)(a)
    `a life estate approved by the Chief Commissioner`                                                   -- (2)(b)
    `a perpetual lease granted by the Commonwealth or the State`                                         -- (2)(c)
    `a Crown lease that may be converted into an estate in fee simple`                                   -- (2)(d)
    `a purchaser's interest in an instalment purchase of fee simple from the Commonwealth or the State`  -- (2)(e)
    `a purchaser's interest in fee simple under a terms contract`                                        -- (2)(e1)
    `a Crown licence or right of occupancy giving reasonable security of tenure in the Chief Commissioner's opinion` -- (2)(f)
    `company shares or trust units for exclusive occupation, as the Chief Commissioner is satisfied`     -- (2)(g)
    `some other interest, such as an ordinary lease or a tenancy`

-- s 5(3): "(a) an interest is not a relevant interest at a particular time unless the holder of the interest has, or will
-- have within 12 months after that time (or a longer time allowed by the Chief Commissioner), a right to immediate
-- occupation of the land, and (b) an interest is not a relevant interest in the hands of a person who holds it subject to
-- a trust." (6): a guardian's holding for a person under a legal disability is not encoded (s 16 is out).
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of interest in land`
      `a right to immediate occupation within 12 months or the longer time allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `held subject to a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a relevant interest` IF
        CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `some other interest, such as an ordinary lease or a tenancy` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    AND `a right to immediate occupation within 12 months or the longer time allowed`
    AND (NOT `held subject to a trust`)

§§ `s 6 -- spouses`

-- s 6(1): "A person is the spouse of another person if, on the commencement date of the eligible transaction-- (a) they
-- are legally married, or (b) the person is the de facto partner of the other person." "De facto partner" is defined in
-- s 21C of the Interpretation Act 1987, which is not deposited: it is asked as a fact. s 6(2): a person to whom the
-- applicant is legally married is not the applicant's spouse "if the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that-- (a) the
-- applicant was not cohabiting with the person on the commencement date ..., and (b) at the time of deciding the
-- application, the applicant is not cohabiting with the person and has no intention of resuming cohabitation."
DECLARE `Partner` HAS
    `is legally married to the applicant on the commencement date`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the applicant's de facto partner on the commencement date`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that they were not cohabiting and will not resume`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the partner's history`                                                                              IS AN `Earlier history`

GIVEN `married` IS A BOOLEAN, `de facto` IS A BOOLEAN, `apart` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `they are spouses` IF
        (`married` AND (NOT `apart`))
    OR  `de facto`

GIVEN `p` IS A `Partner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the applicant's spouse` IF
    `they are spouses` (`p`'s `is legally married to the applicant on the commencement date`) (`p`'s `is the applicant's de facto partner on the commencement date`) (`p`'s `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that they were not cohabiting and will not resume`)

§§ `ss 10 and 11 -- the earlier history of the applicant and the applicant's spouse`

-- Facts about another State or a Territory. Whether an interest or a grant there counts is a question of that place's
-- "corresponding law" (s 3), which is not deposited; `depends on the corresponding law` makes the answer `not covered`.
DECLARE `Interstate fact` IS ONE OF
    `does not apply`
    `applies under the corresponding law`
    `depends on the corresponding law`

GIVEN `f` IS AN `Interstate fact`
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`the answer for` `f` MEANS
    CONSIDER `f`
    WHEN `does not apply` THEN `answered` FALSE
    WHEN `applies under the corresponding law` THEN `answered` TRUE
    WHEN `depends on the corresponding law` THEN `not covered` `it turns on the corresponding law of another State or a Territory, which is not deposited`

-- s 10(1): "(a) the applicant or the applicant's spouse has been a party to an earlier application under this Act or a
-- corresponding law, and (b) a grant was paid on the application." (2): "not ineligible if the grant was paid but later
-- paid back, together with any penalty payable under section 45."
-- s 11(1): "has, before 1 July 2000, held-- (a) a relevant interest in residential property in New South Wales, or (b) an
-- interest in residential property in another State or a Territory that is a relevant interest under the corresponding law
-- of that State or Territory." (2): a deferment of the right of occupation because the property was leased is disregarded.
-- (3): "at any time before the commencement date ... (a) held a relevant interest in residential property in New South
-- Wales or [such an interest elsewhere], and (b) occupied the property as a place of residence for a continuous period of
-- at least 6 months."
-- s 3: land is "residential property" if there is on it "a building ... lawfully occupied as a place of residence or
-- suitable for occupation as a place of residence". "Relevant interest" is s 5 (see `it is a relevant interest`).
DECLARE `Earlier history` HAS
    `a party to an earlier application under this Act on which a grant was paid`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `a party to an earlier application under a corresponding law on which a grant was paid`              IS AN `Interstate fact`
    `every such grant was paid back with any penalty payable under s 45`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `held a relevant interest in residential property in New South Wales before 1 July 2000`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `held a relevant interest in residential property elsewhere in Australia before 1 July 2000`          IS AN `Interstate fact`
    `held a relevant interest in residential property in New South Wales and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `held a relevant interest in residential property elsewhere in Australia and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS AN `Interstate fact`

GIVEN `h` IS AN `Earlier history`
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`an unrepaid earlier grant in` `h` MEANS
    `a grant was paid` `and also` `it was not paid back`
    WHERE
        `a grant was paid` MEANS (`known` (`h`'s `a party to an earlier application under this Act on which a grant was paid`)) `or else` (`the answer for` (`h`'s `a party to an earlier application under a corresponding law on which a grant was paid`))
        `it was not paid back` MEANS `known` (NOT (`h`'s `every such grant was paid back with any penalty payable under s 45`))

GIVEN `h` IS AN `Earlier history`
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`an earlier home that counts in` `h` MEANS
    `any of` (LIST `known` (`h`'s `held a relevant interest in residential property in New South Wales before 1 July 2000`),
                   `the answer for` (`h`'s `held a relevant interest in residential property elsewhere in Australia before 1 July 2000`),
                   `known` (`h`'s `held a relevant interest in residential property in New South Wales and lived in it for 6 continuous months`),
                   `the answer for` (`h`'s `held a relevant interest in residential property elsewhere in Australia and lived in it for 6 continuous months`))

§§ `s 12 -- residence`

-- s 12(1): the applicant must "(a) commence occupation of the home ... as the applicant's principal place of residence
-- within 12 months after completion of the eligible transaction or the period approved by the Chief Commissioner under
-- this section, and (b) occupy the home as a principal place of residence for a continuous period of at least 12 months
-- or the period approved". (3): the Chief Commissioner may approve a later start or a shorter period; (4) may exempt;
-- (5) may do so "at any time". The approvals and the exemption are facts: each covers the applicant's own start or stay.
DECLARE `Residence` HAS
    `occupies the home as principal place of residence`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date occupation began`                                               IS A DATE
    `continuous months of occupation`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `the Chief Commissioner approved the later start`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Chief Commissioner approved the shorter period`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Chief Commissioner exempted the applicant from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 12(1)(a), (b) with s 12(3).
GIVEN `the day of completion` IS A DATE, `r` IS A `Residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant complies with the residence requirement` IF
        `r`'s `occupies the home as principal place of residence`
    AND (    `r`'s `the date occupation began` `is on or before` (`12 months after` `the day of completion`)
         OR  `r`'s `the Chief Commissioner approved the later start`)
    AND (    `r`'s `continuous months of occupation` AT LEAST 12
         OR  `r`'s `the Chief Commissioner approved the shorter period`)

§§ `The application`

-- s 9(1): "an Australian citizen or a permanent resident on the commencement date". s 3: "permanent resident means--
-- (a) the holder of a permanent visa within the meaning of section 30 of the Migration Act 1958 of the Commonwealth, or
-- (b) a New Zealand citizen who holds a special category visa within the meaning of section 32" of that Act. Citizenship
-- (Australian Citizenship Act 2007) and the visas are Commonwealth terms, asked as facts.
DECLARE `Status on the commencement date` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian citizen`
    `the holder of a permanent visa`
    `a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa`
    `none of these`

-- One applicant. s 8A(1) does not say on what day the applicant must be 18; READING: on the day the application is made.
DECLARE `Applicant` HAS
    `is a natural person`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `age when applying`                            IS A NUMBER
    `exempted from the age requirement`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `status`                                       IS A `Status on the commencement date`
    `the applicant's history`                      IS AN `Earlier history`
    `the applicant's partners`                     IS A LIST OF `Partner`
    `the applicant's residence`                    IS A `Residence`

-- s 13(1)(a)-(c): the three kinds of eligible transaction.
DECLARE `Kind of transaction` IS ONE OF
    `a contract for the purchase of a home`
    `a comprehensive home building contract`
    `the building of a home by an owner builder`

-- s 13(3A) and Schedule 1 cll 19, 20(3), 22(2): whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract "replaces a
-- contract made before" a date, for "the same home" or "the same or a substantially similar home".
DECLARE `Replaced contract` IS ONE OF
    `it replaces no earlier contract`
    `it replaces a contract made before 1 October 2012`
    `it replaces a contract made from 1 October 2012 to 30 June 2017`

-- s 13A(4): the regulations "may prescribe a different amount as the eligibility cap". None is deposited.
DECLARE `Cap regulation` IS ONE OF
    `no regulation under s 13A(4) applies`
    `a regulation under s 13A(4) prescribes` HAS `the prescribed cap` IS A NUMBER
    `a regulation under s 13A(4) applies but its amount is not known`

-- One case is one eligible transaction (s 7(4): "Only one first home owner grant is payable for the same eligible
-- transaction").
-- `the commencement date`: s 13(4): for a contract, "the date when the contract is made"; for an owner builder, "the date
-- when laying the foundations for the home commences" or "another date the Chief Commissioner considers appropriate".
-- `the completion date` (actual or expected) and `has been completed`: s 13(5): a purchase is completed when the
-- purchaser "becomes entitled to possession" and, except under a terms contract, a registrable interest "is registered";
-- a building contract or owner build when "the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence".
-- `the consideration`: s 13(7): the price; "the total consideration payable for the building work"; or the owner
-- builder's "actual costs ... (excluding any allowance for the owner builder's own labour)".
-- `the unencumbered value of the property or home`: s 13B(1)(a)(ii), (c)(i), (3): for a purchase, the property at the
-- commencement date; for an owner build, the home at completion; valued disregarding encumbrances, arrangements not at
-- arm's length, and schemes to reduce the value.
-- `the consideration for the land`, `the unencumbered value of the land`: s 13B(2), for a building contract (at the
-- commencement date) or an owner build (at completion).
DECLARE `Transaction` HAS
    `kind`                                                           IS A `Kind of transaction`
    `the home is in New South Wales`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commencement date`                                          IS A DATE
    `the completion date`                                            IS A DATE
    `has been completed`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `origin of the home`                                             IS AN `Origin of the home`
    `the home has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner occupied the demolished premises`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person building is or will on completion be the owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an option or right granted before 1 July 2000 applies`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `replaced contract`                                              IS A `Replaced contract`
    `made pursuant to an option granted in the transitional period`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consideration`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the unencumbered value of the property or home`                 IS A NUMBER
    `the consideration for the land`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the unencumbered value of the land`                             IS A NUMBER
    `cap regulation`                                                 IS A `Cap regulation`
    `a grant has already been paid for this transaction`             IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 15: the owners on completion who do not apply are described by two numbers (see `all interested persons are
-- applicants`). `the Chief Commissioner has authorised payment before completion`: s 7(3), s 20(1)(a).
DECLARE `Application` HAS
    `the applicants`                                                 IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
    `the transaction`                                                IS A `Transaction`
    `the largest ownership share of an owner who is not applying`    IS A NUMBER
    `the total ownership share of all small interest holders`        IS A NUMBER
    `the Chief Commissioner has authorised payment before completion` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `s 15 -- all interested persons to join in the application`

-- s 15(1): "All interested persons must be applicants." (2): an interested person is one who "is, or will be, on the
-- completion of the eligible transaction ..., an owner of the relevant home" (s 5), but not (a)-(d), (f) (the fee simple
-- owner under ss 6C, 6D; other buyers under a multiple occupancy contract or on multiple occupancy land; the NSW Land and
-- Housing Corporation; an approved equity partner under the Duties Act 1997), nor "(e) a person whose ownership share in
-- the relevant home does not exceed 5% (a small interest holder), but only if, in a case where there is more than one
-- small interest holder, the total ownership share of all small interest holders in the relevant home does not exceed 5%".
-- Owners excluded by (a)-(d) or (f) are left out of both numbers. `the largest ownership share of an owner who is not
-- applying` is 0 when every other owner applies. Where there is one small interest holder, the total is that holder's own
-- share, which is 5% or less by definition, so the total test can be applied in every case (NOTES.md finding 7).
GIVEN `largest share not applying` IS A NUMBER, `total small share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every owner who is not applying is excluded from being an interested person` IF
        `largest share not applying` EQUALS 0
    OR  (`largest share not applying` AT MOST 5 AND `total small share` AT MOST 5)

GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `all interested persons are applicants` IF
    `every owner who is not applying is excluded from being an interested person` (`the application`'s `the largest ownership share of an owner who is not applying`) (`the application`'s `the total ownership share of all small interest holders`)

§§ `Part 2 Division 2 -- the eligibility criteria`

-- s 8: "An applicant for a first home owner grant must be a natural person."
GIVEN `a` IS AN `Applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `criterion 1 is met by` `a` IF `a`'s `is a natural person`

-- s 8A(1): "must be at least 18 years of age". (2): the Chief Commissioner "may exempt" an applicant if satisfied the
-- home will be the applicant's principal place of residence within 12 months of completion and the application is not
-- part of a scheme to circumvent the limits. The exemption is a fact.
GIVEN `a` IS AN `Applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `criterion 1A is met by` `a` IF
    `a`'s `age when applying` AT LEAST 18 OR `a`'s `exempted from the age requirement`

GIVEN `a` IS AN `Applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a citizen or permanent resident on the commencement date` IF
    CONSIDER `a`'s `status`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `applicants` IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there are joint applicants` IF count `applicants` AT LEAST 2

-- s 9(1): citizen or permanent resident on the commencement date. (2): "If an application is made by joint applicants
-- and at least one (but not all) of the applicants complies with the requirement ..., the non-complying applicant or
-- applicants are exempted".
GIVEN `a` IS AN `Applicant`, `applicants` IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `criterion 2 is met by` `a` `among` `applicants` IF
        `is a citizen or permanent resident on the commencement date` `a`
    OR  (    `there are joint applicants` `applicants`
         AND any (GIVEN `x` YIELD `is a citizen or permanent resident on the commencement date` `x`) `applicants`)

-- ss 10, 11: the histories that count against an applicant are the applicant's own and each spouse's.
GIVEN `a` IS AN `Applicant`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Earlier history`
`the histories that count against` `a` MEANS
    `a`'s `the applicant's history` FOLLOWED BY
        map (GIVEN `p` YIELD `p`'s `the partner's history`) (filter `is the applicant's spouse` (`a`'s `the applicant's partners`))

-- s 10: criterion 3.
GIVEN `a` IS AN `Applicant`
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`criterion 3 is met by` `a` MEANS
    `the opposite of` (`any of` (map `an unrepaid earlier grant in` (`the histories that count against` `a`)))

-- s 11: criterion 4.
GIVEN `a` IS AN `Applicant`
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`criterion 4 is met by` `a` MEANS
    `the opposite of` (`any of` (map `an earlier home that counts in` (`the histories that count against` `a`)))

-- s 12: criterion 5. (4): the Chief Commissioner may exempt. (6): "If an application is made by joint applicants and at
-- least one (but not all) of the applicants complies with the residence requirement, the non-complying applicant or
-- applicants are exempted".
GIVEN `a`                 IS AN `Applicant`
      `applicants`        IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
      `the day of completion` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `criterion 5 is met by` `a` `among` `applicants` `completing on` `the day of completion` IF
        `the applicant complies with the residence requirement` `the day of completion` (`a`'s `the applicant's residence`)
    OR  `a`'s `the applicant's residence`'s `the Chief Commissioner exempted the applicant from the residence requirement`
    OR  (    `there are joint applicants` `applicants`
         AND any (GIVEN `x` YIELD `the applicant complies with the residence requirement` `the day of completion` (`x`'s `the applicant's residence`)) `applicants`)

-- s 7(1)(a), (2): the applicant "complies with the eligibility criteria", allowing the exemptions the Act gives.
GIVEN `a` IS AN `Applicant`, `the application` IS AN `Application`
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`the eligibility criteria are met by` `a` `on` `the application` MEANS
    `all of` (LIST `known` (`criterion 1 is met by` `a`),
                   `known` (`criterion 1A is met by` `a`),
                   `known` (`criterion 2 is met by` `a` `among` (`the application`'s `the applicants`)),
                   `criterion 3 is met by` `a`,
                   `criterion 4 is met by` `a`,
                   `known` (`criterion 5 is met by` `a` `among` (`the application`'s `the applicants`) `completing on` (`the application`'s `the transaction`'s `the completion date`)))

-- s 7(1)(a): "the applicant or, if there are 2 or more of them, each of the applicants complies with the eligibility
-- criteria".
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application`
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`each applicant meets the eligibility criteria on` `the application` MEANS
    `there is an applicant` `and also` (`all of` `each applicant's answer`)
    WHERE
        `there is an applicant` MEANS `known` (count (`the application`'s `the applicants`) AT LEAST 1)
        `each applicant's answer` MEANS map (GIVEN `a` YIELD `the eligibility criteria are met by` `a` `on` `the application`) (`the application`'s `the applicants`)

-- s 20(3): "if the residence requirement is not complied with". READING: it is not complied with when some applicant does
-- not meet criterion 5, allowing the s 12(4) and (6) exemptions.
GIVEN `applicants` IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
      `the day of completion` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the residence requirement is not complied with by` `applicants` `completing on` `the day of completion` IF
    any (GIVEN `a` YIELD NOT (`criterion 5 is met by` `a` `among` `applicants` `completing on` `the day of completion`)) `applicants`

GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the residence requirement is not complied with on` `the application` IF
    `the residence requirement is not complied with by` (`the application`'s `the applicants`) `completing on` (`the application`'s `the transaction`'s `the completion date`)

§§ `Part 2 Division 3 -- eligible transactions`

-- Schedule 1 cll 18, 19, 20(3), 22(2): when the earlier law governs, every answer about the transaction is `not covered`.
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Why not covered`
`the earlier law governs` `t` MEANS
    CONSIDER `t`'s `replaced contract`
    WHEN `it replaces no earlier contract` THEN
        IF `t`'s `the commencement date` `is before` `1 October 2012`
        THEN JUST `the commencement date is before 1 October 2012, and Schedule 1 Part 11 keeps the earlier Part 2, which is not deposited`
        ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces one made before 1 July 2017, and Schedule 1 keeps the earlier law, which is not encoded`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the home is a new home in` `t` IF
    `it is a new home` (`t`'s `origin of the home`) (`t`'s `the home has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`) (`t`'s `the owner occupied the demolished premises`)

-- s 13(1): "(a) a contract made on or after 1 October 2012 for the purchase of a new home in New South Wales, or (b) a
-- comprehensive home building contract made on or after 1 October 2012 by the owner of land in New South Wales, or by a
-- person who will on completion of the contract be the owner of land in New South Wales, to have a new home built on the
-- land, or (c) the building of a new home in New South Wales by an owner builder if the building work commences on or
-- after 1 October 2012." s 3: an owner builder is "an owner of land who builds a home". (3): a contract under "an option
-- to purchase ... granted before" 1 July 2000, or a building contract under "a right or option granted before that date",
-- is not an eligible transaction. READING: the owner builder's building work commences on the s 13(4)(b) commencement date.
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an eligible transaction under the current Part 2` IF
        `t`'s `the home is in New South Wales`
    AND `the home is a new home in` `t`
    AND (NOT (`t`'s `the commencement date` `is before` `1 October 2012`))
    AND CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
        WHEN `a contract for the purchase of a home` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `t`'s `the person building is or will on completion be the owner of the land`
    AND (NOT (`t`'s `an option or right granted before 1 July 2000 applies`))

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`is an eligible transaction` `t` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier law governs` `t`
    WHEN JUST `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `answered` (`it is an eligible transaction under the current Part 2` `t`)

-- s 13AA(2): "A first home builder's grant is available ... only for ... (a) a comprehensive home building contract, (b)
-- the building of a home by an owner builder." (3): "A first home purchaser's grant is available ... for any other
-- eligible transaction." (4): only one type for the same transaction.
DECLARE `Type of grant` IS ONE OF
    `a first home builder's grant`
    `a first home purchaser's grant`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A `Type of grant`
`the type of grant available for` `t` MEANS
    CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
    WHEN `a contract for the purchase of a home` THEN `a first home purchaser's grant`
    OTHERWISE `a first home builder's grant`

-- s 13A(2): "(a) $750,000 for a first home builder's grant, (b) $600,000 for a first home purchaser's grant." (4): a
-- regulation may prescribe a different amount. (5): the section applies to a commencement date "on or after 1 July 2017".
GIVEN `the type` IS A `Type of grant`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 13A(2) cap for` `the type` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the type`
    WHEN `a first home builder's grant` THEN 750000
    WHEN `a first home purchaser's grant` THEN 600000

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the eligibility cap for` `t` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier law governs` `t`
    WHEN JUST `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `t`'s `the commencement date` `is before` `1 July 2017`
        THEN `not covered` `the commencement date is before 1 July 2017, and Schedule 1 keeps the earlier eligibility caps, which are not encoded`
        ELSE CONSIDER `t`'s `cap regulation`
             WHEN `no regulation under s 13A(4) applies` THEN `answered` (`the s 13A(2) cap for` (`the type of grant available for` `t`))
             WHEN `a regulation under s 13A(4) prescribes` `the cap` THEN `answered` `the cap`
             WHEN `a regulation under s 13A(4) applies but its amount is not known` THEN `not covered` `a regulation under s 13A(4) sets a different eligibility cap, and its amount was not given (no regulation is deposited)`

-- s 13B(1): total value is "(a) [for a purchase] the greater of ... (i) the consideration ..., (ii) the unencumbered
-- value, at the commencement date, of the property", "(b) [for a building contract] ... (i) the consideration ..., and
-- (ii) the value, at the commencement date, of the relevant interest in the land", "(c) [for an owner builder] ... (i) the
-- unencumbered value, at the date the transaction is completed, of the home, and (ii) the value, at [that] date ..., of
-- the relevant interest in the land". (2): the land's value "is the greater of ... (a) the consideration paid or payable
-- for the interest, (b) the unencumbered value of the interest."
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the relevant interest in the land in` `t` MEANS
    max (`t`'s `the consideration for the land`) (`t`'s `the unencumbered value of the land`)

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total value of` `t` MEANS
    CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
    WHEN `a contract for the purchase of a home` THEN
        max (`t`'s `the consideration`) (`t`'s `the unencumbered value of the property or home`)
    WHEN `a comprehensive home building contract` THEN
        `t`'s `the consideration` PLUS `the value of the relevant interest in the land in` `t`
    WHEN `the building of a home by an owner builder` THEN
        `t`'s `the unencumbered value of the property or home` PLUS `the value of the relevant interest in the land in` `t`

-- s 13A(1) and s 7(1)(c): "the total value of the transaction does not exceed the eligibility cap".
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`the total value is within the eligibility cap for` `t` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the eligibility cap for` `t`
    WHEN `answered` `the cap` THEN `answered` (`the total value of` `t` AT MOST `the cap`)
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`

§§ `s 7 -- entitlement to the grant`

-- s 7(1): "A first home owner grant is payable on an application under this Act if-- (a) the applicant or ... each of the
-- applicants complies with the eligibility criteria, and (b) the transaction ... (i) is an eligible transaction, and (ii)
-- has been completed, and (c) the total value of the transaction does not exceed the eligibility cap". (3): "payable
-- before completion ... if payment is authorised under section 20". (4): "Only one first home owner grant is payable for
-- the same eligible transaction." s 15(1): "All interested persons must be applicants."
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application`
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`the grant is payable on` `the application` MEANS
    `all of` (LIST `each applicant meets the eligibility criteria on` `the application`,
                   `is an eligible transaction` `t`,
                   `known` (`t`'s `has been completed` OR `the application`'s `the Chief Commissioner has authorised payment before completion`),
                   `the total value is within the eligibility cap for` `t`,
                   `known` (NOT (`t`'s `a grant has already been paid for this transaction`)),
                   `known` (`all interested persons are applicants` `the application`))
    WHERE
        `t` MEANS `the application`'s `the transaction`

§§ `s 18 -- the amount of the grant`

-- s 18(1): "(a) ... a commencement date on or after 1 October 2012 but before 1 January 2016--$15,000, or (b) ... a
-- commencement date on or after 1 January 2016--$10,000." (2): "For an eligible transaction with a commencement date on or
-- after 1 October 2012 that is a contract for the purchase of a home, or a comprehensive home building contract, made
-- pursuant to an option granted in the transitional period, the amount of the grant is $7,000." (5): the transitional
-- period starts on the day the Bill for the 2012 Budget Measures Act "was introduced in the Legislative Assembly"; that day
-- is not in the deposit, so whether the option falls in it is a fact. (4): "The maximum amount of the first home owner
-- grant is the consideration for the eligible transaction."
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 18 amount before the cap at the consideration for` `t` MEANS
    IF      `t`'s `made pursuant to an option granted in the transitional period`
        AND CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
            WHEN `the building of a home by an owner builder` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
    THEN 7000
    ELSE IF `t`'s `the commencement date` `is before` `1 January 2016`
         THEN 15000
         ELSE 10000

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the amount of the grant for` `t` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier law governs` `t`
    WHEN JUST `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `answered` (min (`the s 18 amount before the cap at the consideration for` `t`) (`t`'s `the consideration`))

-- The amount payable on an application: the s 18 amount if s 7 makes the grant payable, otherwise nothing.
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the grant payable on` `the application` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the grant is payable on` `the application`
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
    WHEN `answered` `payable` THEN
        IF `payable` THEN `the amount of the grant for` (`the application`'s `the transaction`) ELSE `answered` 0

§§ `s 14(5), (6) -- the application period`

-- s 14(5): "An application may only be made within a period (the application period)-- (a) commencing on the commencement
-- date of the eligible transaction ..., and (b) ending 12 months after the completion of the eligible transaction".
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`
GIVETH A DATE
`the application period ends on` `t` MEANS `12 months after` (`t`'s `the completion date`)

-- s 14(6): "the Chief Commissioner has a discretion to allow an application before or after the application period."
GIVEN `the day of application` IS A DATE, `t` IS A `Transaction`, `the Chief Commissioner allows it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application may be made on` `the day of application` `for` `t` `if allowed` `the Chief Commissioner allows it` IF
        (    `t`'s `the commencement date` `is on or before` `the day of application`
         AND (`the day of application` `is on or before` (`the application period ends on` `t`)))
    OR  `the Chief Commissioner allows it`

§§ `ss 20 and 45 -- the dates in the conditions of an advance payment`

-- s 20(2), (2A), (3): "within 14 days after" the day the condition is broken.
`the days allowed to give notice and repay` MEANS 14

-- s 20(2): "if the transaction is not completed within 12 months of the commencement of the transaction or a longer
-- period allowed by the Chief Commissioner". `the longer period allowed ends on` is NOTHING if none was allowed.
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`, `the longer period allowed ends on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the period for completion ends on` `t` `or` `the longer period allowed ends on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the longer period allowed ends on`
    WHEN JUST `the day` THEN `the day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `12 months after` (`t`'s `the commencement date`)

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction`, `the longer period allowed ends on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it was not completed within the period in` `t` `or` `the longer period allowed ends on` IF
    NOT (    `t`'s `has been completed`
         AND (`t`'s `the completion date` `is on or before` (`the period for completion ends on` `t` `or` `the longer period allowed ends on`)))

-- s 20(3): "within 14 days after the end of the period allowed for compliance". The Act does not say when that period
-- ends. READING: if the applicant did not begin occupation in time, at the end of the time allowed to begin (12 months
-- after completion); if the applicant began in time but did not stay, 12 months after occupation began, when the
-- required continuous period would have ended (NOTES.md finding 11).
GIVEN `the day of completion` IS A DATE, `r` IS A `Residence`
GIVETH A DATE
`the period allowed for compliance with the residence requirement ends on` MEANS
    IF      `r`'s `occupies the home as principal place of residence`
        AND (    `r`'s `the date occupation began` `is on or before` (`12 months after` `the day of completion`)
             OR  `r`'s `the Chief Commissioner approved the later start`)
    THEN `12 months after` (`r`'s `the date occupation began`)
    ELSE `12 months after` `the day of completion`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give notice and repay after` `the day` MEANS `the day` `plus` `the days allowed to give notice and repay` `days`

-- s 20(4), s 21(4): "A person who fails to comply with the condition ... is guilty of an offence. Maximum penalty ...: 50
-- penalty units." The value of a penalty unit is set by another Act, not deposited.
`the maximum fine, in penalty units, for failing to comply with a condition of the grant` MEANS 50

§§ `s 45 -- repayment and penalty`

-- s 45(1): the Chief Commissioner "may, by written notice ..., require the person for whom an amount was paid under this
-- Act to repay the amount if-- (a) the amount was paid in error, or (b) the Chief Commissioner reverses the decision under
-- which the amount was paid for another reason." The conditions of an advance payment require repayment of themselves
-- (s 20(2), (2A), (3)).
GIVEN `paid in error` IS A BOOLEAN, `the decision was reversed` IS A BOOLEAN, `a condition of the grant requires repayment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `repayment can be required` IF
    `paid in error` OR `the decision was reversed` OR `a condition of the grant requires repayment`

-- s 45(2): "The Chief Commissioner may impose a penalty not exceeding the amount the person is required to repay if-- (a)
-- the amount was paid under a first home owner grant as a result of dishonesty by an applicant ..., or ... (c) the person
-- fails to make a repayment required-- (i) under this section, or (ii) by the conditions of a first home owner grant."
GIVEN `the amount required to be repaid` IS A NUMBER, `paid as a result of dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN, `a required repayment was not made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most penalty under s 45(2)` MEANS
    IF `paid as a result of dishonesty` OR `a required repayment was not made`
    THEN `the amount required to be repaid`
    ELSE 0

§§ `Regulative rules -- the applicants and the Chief Commissioner`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day each rule says. Joint applicants are numbered 1, 2, ... on the application.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `applicant` HAS `number` IS A NUMBER
    `the Chief Commissioner`

DECLARE `Action` IS ONE OF
    `apply for the grant`
    `give the Chief Commissioner written notice`
    `repay the amount of the grant`
    `require repayment by written notice`
    `impose a penalty` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER

-- s 21(3): "In the case of a joint application, each applicant is individually liable to comply with a requirement ...
-- but compliance by any one or more of them is to be regarded as compliance by both or all." Each joint applicant is
-- bound (each side of the ROR breaches); any one's act fulfils all. READING: the same is applied to the statutory
-- conditions in s 20, which s 21(3) does not name, since otherwise each joint applicant would owe the whole grant back
-- (NOTES.md finding 12).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the act` IS AN `Action`, `days` IS A NUMBER, `why` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`one of applicants 1 to` `n` `must` `the act` `within` `days` `lest` `why` MEANS
    IF `n` AT MOST 1
    THEN PARTY `applicant` 1
         MUST   EXACTLY `the act`
         WITHIN `days`
         LEST   BREACH BY `applicant` 1 BECAUSE `why`
    ELSE (PARTY `applicant` `n`
          MUST   EXACTLY `the act`
          WITHIN `days`
          LEST   BREACH BY `applicant` `n` BECAUSE `why`)
         ROR (`one of applicants 1 to` (`n` MINUS 1) `must` `the act` `within` `days` `lest` `why`)

-- The notice-and-repay pair common to s 20(2), (2A) and (3).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `why` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`the applicants must give notice and repay within 14 days` `n` `lest` `why` MEANS
        (`one of applicants 1 to` `n` `must` `give the Chief Commissioner written notice` `within` `the days allowed to give notice and repay` `lest` `why`)
    RAND (`one of applicants 1 to` `n` `must` `repay the amount of the grant` `within` `the days allowed to give notice and repay` `lest` `why`)

-- s 14(5), (6): the application period. Clock: day 0 is the commencement date; `days in the application period` runs to
-- 12 months after completion. Nobody is obliged to apply, so the rule is DO, not MUST: its BREACH marks that the right to
-- apply has been lost, not an offence. If the Chief Commissioner allows an application outside the period (s 14(6)), it
-- may be made at any time.
GIVEN `the person applying` IS A `Party`, `days in the application period` IS A NUMBER, `the Chief Commissioner allows an application outside the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`s 14(5), (6) -- an application may only be made within the application period` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Commissioner allows an application outside the period`
    THEN PARTY `the person applying`
         MAY   `apply for the grant`
    ELSE PARTY `the person applying`
         DO     `apply for the grant`
         WITHIN `days in the application period`
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the person applying` BECAUSE "s 14(5): the application period has ended (12 months after completion); an application may now be made only if the Chief Commissioner allows it under s 14(6)"

-- s 20(2): "If a first home owner grant is paid before completion ..., the payment is made on condition that, if the
-- transaction is not completed within 12 months of the commencement of the transaction or a longer period allowed by the
-- Chief Commissioner, the applicant must within 14 days after the end of the period concerned-- (a) give written notice
-- of that fact to the Chief Commissioner, and (b) repay the amount of the grant." (4): failing to comply "is guilty of an
-- offence", maximum 50 penalty units. Clock: day 0 is the end of the period concerned.
GIVEN `the number of applicants` IS A NUMBER, `paid before completion` IS A BOOLEAN, `not completed within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`s 20(2) -- paid before completion, and not completed in time: give notice and repay within 14 days` MEANS
    IF `paid before completion` AND `not completed within the period`
    THEN `the applicants must give notice and repay within 14 days` `the number of applicants` `lest` "s 20(2), (4): the transaction was not completed within the period; notice and repayment were due within 14 days. An offence (maximum 50 penalty units); the Chief Commissioner may also impose a penalty up to the amount to be repaid (s 45(2)(c)(ii))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 20(2A): "If the first home owner grant is paid in anticipation of compliance with the eligibility cap, the payment is
-- made on condition that, if the applicant becomes aware that the total value of the transaction exceeds or will exceed
-- the eligibility cap, the applicant must within 14 days after the day on which the applicant becomes so aware-- (a) give
-- written notice ..., and (b) repay the amount of the grant." Clock: day 0 is the day the applicant becomes aware.
GIVEN `the number of applicants` IS A NUMBER, `paid in anticipation of compliance with the cap` IS A BOOLEAN, `the total value exceeds or will exceed the cap` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`s 20(2A) -- paid in anticipation of the cap, and over it: give notice and repay within 14 days` MEANS
    IF `paid in anticipation of compliance with the cap` AND `the total value exceeds or will exceed the cap`
    THEN `the applicants must give notice and repay within 14 days` `the number of applicants` `lest` "s 20(2A), (4): the total value exceeds or will exceed the eligibility cap; notice and repayment were due within 14 days of becoming aware. An offence (maximum 50 penalty units); the Chief Commissioner may also impose a penalty up to the amount to be repaid (s 45(2)(c)(ii))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 20(3): "If a first home owner grant is paid in anticipation of compliance with the residence requirement, the
-- payment is made on condition that, if the residence requirement is not complied with, the applicant must within 14 days
-- after the end of the period allowed for compliance-- (a) give written notice ..., and (b) repay the amount of the
-- grant." Clock: day 0 is the end of the period allowed for compliance.
GIVEN `the number of applicants` IS A NUMBER, `paid in anticipation of the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN, `the residence requirement is not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`s 20(3) -- paid in anticipation of residence, and not complied with: give notice and repay within 14 days` MEANS
    IF `paid in anticipation of the residence requirement` AND `the residence requirement is not complied with`
    THEN `the applicants must give notice and repay within 14 days` `the number of applicants` `lest` "s 20(3), (4): the residence requirement was not complied with; notice and repayment were due within 14 days after the end of the period allowed for compliance. An offence (maximum 50 penalty units); the Chief Commissioner may also impose a penalty up to the amount to be repaid (s 45(2)(c)(ii))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 21(1), (2): the Chief Commissioner may pay "on conditions the Chief Commissioner considers appropriate", which "may
-- require a person on whose application the first home owner grant is paid-- (a) to give notice of non-compliance with
-- the condition within a period stated in the condition, and (b) to repay the grant or a part of the grant within a period
-- stated in the condition." (3): joint liability. (4): failing to comply is an offence, maximum 50 penalty units. Clock:
-- day 0 is the day of non-compliance; the periods are the ones the condition states.
GIVEN `the number of applicants` IS A NUMBER, `the condition is not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN, `days stated for notice` IS A NUMBER, `days stated for repayment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`s 21(2), (3) -- a condition imposed by the Chief Commissioner: give notice and repay within the stated periods` MEANS
    IF `the condition is not complied with`
    THEN    (`one of applicants 1 to` `the number of applicants` `must` `give the Chief Commissioner written notice` `within` `days stated for notice` `lest` "s 21(2), (4): notice of non-compliance with the condition was not given within the period it states. An offence (maximum 50 penalty units)")
        RAND (`one of applicants 1 to` `the number of applicants` `must` `repay the amount of the grant` `within` `days stated for repayment` `lest` "s 21(2), (4): the grant was not repaid within the period the condition states. An offence (maximum 50 penalty units); the Chief Commissioner may also impose a penalty up to the amount to be repaid (s 45(2)(c)(ii))")
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 45(1): what may be done to the person: a written notice requiring repayment, if the amount was paid in error or the
-- decision was reversed. Without either ground there is no such power.
GIVEN `paid in error` IS A BOOLEAN, `the decision was reversed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`s 45(1) -- the Chief Commissioner may require repayment by written notice` MEANS
    IF `paid in error` OR `the decision was reversed`
    THEN PARTY `the Chief Commissioner`
         MAY   `require repayment by written notice`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 45(2), (3): "a penalty not exceeding the amount the person is required to repay", by notice. A penalty above that
-- amount is not within the power: it does not match the permission (PROVIDED).
GIVEN `the amount required to be repaid` IS A NUMBER, `paid as a result of dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN, `a required repayment was not made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`s 45(2) -- the Chief Commissioner may impose a penalty up to the amount to be repaid` MEANS
    IF `paid as a result of dishonesty` OR `a required repayment was not made`
    THEN PARTY `the Chief Commissioner`
         MAY   `impose a penalty` `the penalty` PROVIDED `the penalty` AT MOST `the amount required to be repaid`
    ELSE FULFILLED
